{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/901","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/901/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/901/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/901/events","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/901","id":5858963547,"node_id":"I_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABXTiwWw","number":901,"title":"73 hydrate records anchor their parent with closeMatch, which §3 step 2 rejects; kg-microbe folds them into the anhydrous parent","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":10,"created_at":"2026-10-15T02:22:14Z","updated_at":"2026-11-04T01:48:54Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Found while reviewing PR #881. #897 is one instance; this is the backlog.\n\n`MAPPING_SEMANTICS.md` §3 step 2 requires the following for a hydrate with no exact ontology term:\n- its own identity (`cas:` or `kgmicrobe.compound:`);\n- a `skos:broadMatch` to the nearest parent;\n- the Rule B1 registry row.\n\nThe #245 ruling rejected `closeMatch` here, and #664 moved four sulfate hydrates off it. Among MAPPED records whose preferred term states a hydrate, counted on #881's head:\n\n| identity | mapping_quality → parent predicate | records |\n|---|---|---:|\n| `cas:` | CLOSE_MATCH → `skos:closeMatch` | 45 (one is `Mgso4h2o`, fixed by #881) |\n| `kgmicrobe.compound:` | CLOSE_MATCH → `skos:closeMatch` | 28 |\n| `cas:` | NARROW_MATCH → `skos:broadMatch` | 12 |\n| `kgmicrobe.compound:` | NARROW_MATCH → `skos:broadMatch` | 7 |\n\nExamples:\n- `cas:` with closeMatch: `Sodium_Deoxycholate_Monohydrate`, `L-Glutamic_Acid_Monopotassium_Salt_Monohydrate`, `Fosmidomycin_Sodium_Salt_Hydrate`;\n- `kgmicrobe.compound:` with closeMatch: `Cocl2_X_4_H2o`, `Na2hpo4_X_3_H2o`, `Fecl2_X_6_H2o`, `Fecl2_X_7_H2o`, `Cu_No32_X_3_H2o`.\n\n**Why it matters:**\n- kg-microbe's consolidator treats `closeMatch` as symmetric (`scripts/consolidate_chemical_mappings.py:1776`, 1829-1873 at 1acb8b61f). It merges the hydrate's label and `other` tokens into the anhydrous parent's record and force-sets the parent's `canonical_name` to the hydrate label; the last row written wins.\n- This comes from reading the code. I did not run kg-microbe or check which of these parents it actually renames.\n\n**Also:**\n- `MAPPING_SEMANTICS.md` (§3 step 2) says 34 hydrate subjects carry the broadMatch pattern. The count above is lower, so the doc or the data has drifted.\n- `Cu_No32_X_3_H2o` keeps a local identity although its own CAS, 10031-43-3 (copper(II) nitrate trihydrate), is on the record. §3 step 2 would make it `cas:10031-43-3`.\n\n**Related:** #696 (BROAD_MATCH publishes closeMatch) and #884 (schema direction of NARROW/BROAD).\n\n**Fix:** a reviewed batch moving these records to NARROW_MATCH, with broadMatch and registry rows through the receipt chain. Check first which of them are SUPPORTED, because changing the bytes cancels approvals (#898).\n\n## History\n\n**How the cohort got here:**\n- #342 (`scripts/regrade_hydrate_to_close_match.py`, in #500 on 2026-08-28) regraded 72 hydrate→anhydrous rows from narrowMatch to closeMatch on purpose. Its reason: narrowMatch claims a subsumption that ChEBI contradicts.\n- That script also took those records out of Rule B1's scope.\n- 72 SSSOM rows still carry `MIM:curator=regrade_hydrate_to_close_match`.\n\n**The later ruling:**\n- The #245 ruling (#735, 2026-09-22) settled the subsumption concern differently. It keeps `skos:broadMatch`, reads it as \"form of\", and forbids projecting it as `subclass_of`.\n- It also records that `closeMatch` was rejected because it carries no direction and drops Rule B1.\n- §3 step 2 has required broadMatch plus the registry row since then.\n- #664 moved four sulfate hydrates back to that shape.\n\n**Decision for maintainers:** these 73 are the #342 cohort the ruling did not migrate, so whether to migrate them is a maintainer decision, not a data error introduced by one PR.\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/901/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/901/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}